course: dictionary
lesson: 13519
title: Impeding: getting in the way
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To impede something is to get in its way and slow it down or make it harder. «The parked van was impeding traffic on the main road.» The van was in the way, so the cars could not move as fast.
explain: Use the clues in the sentence. «A fallen tree impeded the walkers on the mountain path.» Walkers need a clear path, so a fallen tree makes their way harder. If you swap in the everyday word blocking and the sentence still makes sense, then impeding means blocking or holding up.
explain: The word changes its form: impede, impedes, impeded, impeding. Impeding is a formal word, so you will meet it more in news reports and rule books than in everyday talk.
fact: Impeding means getting in the way of something and slowing it down or making it harder.
fact: «A blocked exit impedes escape in a fire, so keep fire exits clear.»
fact: In football and hockey, impeding is a rule-break where a player blocks an opponent without playing the ball, and the referee may give a free kick.
fact: The everyday words for impeding are blocking and holding up.
fact: The forms are impede, impedes, impeded and impeding.
exercise: «The parked van was impeding traffic on the main road.» What does impeding mean here? | Parking for free | Driving very fast | *Blocking and slowing things down | Painting the road
exercise: «The loud music was impeding my reading.» Which everyday word could replace impeding? | Cheering | Copying | Helping | *Blocking
exercise: In football, the referee gives a free kick for impeding. What does impeding mean in sport? | *Blocking an opponent without playing the ball | Running off the pitch for a drink | Kicking the ball out for a throw-in | Scoring a goal with the ball
test: «The thick snow impeded the rescue team.» What does impeded mean? | Covered the team in paint | Melted the ice away | *Got in the way and slowed them down | Helped them go faster
test: «The fallen branch was impeding the bus.» Which everyday words mean nearly the same as impeding? | Waving and singing | Painting and cleaning | *Blocking and holding up | Thanking and cheering
exam: «The man was accused of impeding the police investigation.» What does impeding mean here? | Helping the police find clues | *Making the police search harder | Sleeping through the case | Taking photos of the crime
